course: dictionary
lesson: 15999
title: Vaguely: not clear, or just a little
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Vaguely is an adverb. It tells us how something is done, or how much of something there is. The first meaning is in a way that is not clear or exact. «The man answered vaguely, so we still did not know where he had been.» He did not give a clear answer.
explain: The second meaning is slightly, or a little. «I vaguely remember her name.» means I remember only a little, not clearly. Look at the words around vaguely to pick the right meaning.
explain: Vaguely often goes with words like remember, familiar and answer. «The face looked vaguely familiar.» means it looked a little like someone you know. In your own writing, try not to answer vaguely. Give clear details instead.
fact: Vaguely is an adverb, so it describes how an action happens.
fact: «Vaguely» means in a way that is not clear or exact.
fact: «Vaguely» can also mean slightly or a little.
fact: «Vaguely familiar» means it looks or sounds a little like something you already know.
fact: In writing, clear details help your reader more than vague words.
exercise: «The man answered vaguely, so we still did not know where he had been.» What does vaguely mean here? | In a loud and angry way | In a quick and happy way | *In a way that was not clear or exact
exercise: «The face in the fog looked vaguely familiar.» What does vaguely suggest? | Very old and grey | Completely unknown and strange | *Slightly familiar, a little like someone you know
exercise: «I vaguely remember her name.» Which word could replace vaguely here without changing the meaning much? | with great care | *a little | at once | very loudly
test: «The shape looked vaguely like a horse in the mist.» Which is closest in meaning to vaguely here? | *Only a little, and hard to see clearly | Quickly and clearly | Very slowly and carefully | Happily and loudly
test: Why should you avoid answering vaguely in your own writing? | Because readers like puzzles | Because vague words are always longer | Because it makes your writing louder | *Because clear details help your reader understand
exam: Mia says, «I only vaguely know the way.» What does Mia mean? | She has never heard of the way | *She knows the way a little, but not clearly | She knows the way perfectly well | She is lost in the woods
